	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Migration 9.5 vers 9.6 - pas de demarrage du service sous Archlinux]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=24363#p24363"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Quand j&#039;execute la commande, voila ce qui est repondu :<br />[tonio@tonio-server tmp]$ &quot;/opt/pgsql-9.5/bin/pg_ctl&quot; -w -l &quot;pg_upgrade_server.log&quot; -D &quot;/var/lib/postgres/data-9.5&quot; -o &quot;-p 50432 -b&#160; -c listen_addresses=&#039;&#039; -c unix_socket_permissions=0700 -c unix_socket_directories=&#039;/var/lib/postgres/data-9.5/global&#039;&quot; start</p><p>waiting for server to start.... stopped waiting<br />pg_ctl: could not start server<br />Examine the log output.</p><p>Quand j&#039;examine la log :<br />LOG:&#160; could not open configuration file &quot;/var/lib/postgres/data-9.5/postgresql.conf&quot;: Permission non accordée<br />FATAL:&#160; configuration file &quot;/var/lib/postgres/data-9.5/postgresql.conf&quot; contains errors</p><p>J&#039;ai donc fait un chmod 700 sur le fichier mais j&#039;ai toujours la meme erreur.</p>]]></content>
